WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.440
Another Thing That Doctor Bright Is&nbsp;
Not Allowed To Do At The Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:09.440
No interacting with SCP-5555-J&nbsp;
under any circumstances!

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:15.440
SCP-5555-J is capable of reducing any&nbsp;
living organism to a miniature (or chibi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.120
if you’d prefer) version of itself.&nbsp;
Dr. Bright may claim he is trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.920
make teacup pigs to hand out at the office&nbsp;
as an incentive, but do not fall for it!

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.760
The last time Dr. Bright&nbsp;
was exposed to SCP-5555-J,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.880
the miniature version it produced of him was a&nbsp;
miniature orangutan. He was brought into custody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.280
and proceeded to behave quite poorly with some&nbsp;
of his own bathroom material, and completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.920
destroy the attending researcher’s clothing,&nbsp;
before escaping to wreak even more havoc.&nbsp;

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:48.800
Dr. Bright knows what mini-him did, and he&nbsp;
has lost his 5555-J privileges for good.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.240
Another Thing That Doctor Bright Is&nbsp;
Not Allowed To Do At The Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.600
Dr. Bright is not permitted to try and&nbsp;
solve every single problem with chainsaws.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.360
Chainsaws can be quite helpful when&nbsp;
it comes to certain specific tasks!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.280
They’re great at, for instance, speedily&nbsp;
chopping up lumber or menacing a group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.800
unsuspecting teenagers on a road trip.&nbsp;
However, Dr. Bright would like you to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.600
believe that the application of chainsaws&nbsp;
goes far beyond the realm of reason or safety.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:20.560
Chainsaws should not be used: To trim your hair,&nbsp;
to contain SCP-682, to cut a sandwich, or as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.600
ammunition in a specialized cannon. It was fine&nbsp;
the one time at the company Christmas Party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:32.400
we all had a good laugh, but Doctor Jones will&nbsp;
never get his big toe back. No more chainsaws!

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.440
Another Series of Things Dr. Bright Is Not&nbsp;
Allowed To Do At The SCP Foundation: Claim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.480
he is from an alternate timeline, issue orders&nbsp;
to, quote, “preserve the timeline”, unquote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.920
or to, quote, “corrupt the timeline”, unquote, or&nbsp;
to, quote, “screw those history nerds, “ unquote.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.680
Dr. Bright may be cursed to live for&nbsp;
a very long time, but he is still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.920
sadly, fundamentally attached to our&nbsp;
timeline. He may have watched Loki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.000
recently, but that doesn’t mean he’s a&nbsp;
multi-verse galavanting trickster god.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.720
He only wishes he was.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.720
Another Thing That Dr. Bright Is Not&nbsp;
Allowed To Do At The SCP Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.720
Dr. Bright is not allowed to apply SCP-963&nbsp;
to any major political figures. Again.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.080
So we’ve got some background here. Anyone&nbsp;
who has seen our video on SCP-4444 will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.000
know that a species of aliens almost&nbsp;
destroyed our planet in the year 2000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.760
after they possessed presidential&nbsp;
candidate Al Gore. In order to stop them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.760
Dr. Bright needed to take over the body&nbsp;
of George W. Bush to run against him.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.440
While this was an emergency where&nbsp;
certain risks needed to be taken,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.280
our current geopolitical landscape is&nbsp;
already too wild and too fractious to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.000
risk Dr. Bright ever rising to any kind&nbsp;
of political power. Though if he did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.320
he would probably run on the major campaign&nbsp;
slogan “C’mon, Guys, You’ve Had Worse!”

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:53.680
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed to do:&nbsp;
Dr. Bright can not give SCP-082 song requests!

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:59.280
SCP-082 loves to sing. If there's anything he&nbsp;
loves more than lying and feasting on human flesh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.560
it's busting out a cheerful little&nbsp;
tune from time to time. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.960
as Dr. Bright has shown that he cannot&nbsp;
be respectful of SCP-082's tastes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:13.680
or the comfort of those working around him, he is&nbsp;
not permitted to request any songs from SCP-082.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.560
Fernand was recently reduced to tears when&nbsp;
his rendition of a classic Italian aria was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.800
interrupted by Dr. Bright's repeated&nbsp;
cries of "Do Free Bird!" and he also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.040
expressed discomfort when Dr. Bright told&nbsp;
him to perform "Like a Virgin." He should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.160
know by now that Fernand only likes to&nbsp;
sing one Madonna song, and it's "Vogue."

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.040
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed to do:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.080
Dr. Bright is not allowed to "accidentally"&nbsp;
spill green gelatin on a dead body.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:46.800
It is well known by SCP staff, particularly those&nbsp;
in the O5 council, that allowing SCP-447's green&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.640
slime to come into contact with a dead body will&nbsp;
result in disaster on a catastrophic scale. Of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:57.120
course, Dr. Bright decided that it would be&nbsp;
hilarious to procure some lime jello from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:03.440
canteen, pretend to trip and fall, and spill the&nbsp;
gelatin all over a body being observed by the O5.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.440
Admittedly, the first time, it was a bit&nbsp;
funny. But it was also extremely stressful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.680
multiple staff fainted, and O5-2 made&nbsp;
it a point to tell Dr. Bright that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:17.440
"owed him a new pair of khakis" after the&nbsp;
sudden terror had made him, well, ruin his.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.680
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.320
Dr. Bright is not allowed to Speed Date!

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.800
If you remember an event called SCP Speed dating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:30.960
please report to Site Command immediately&nbsp;
for your mandatory dose of Class A Amnestic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.280
This event never officially took place, and&nbsp;
there is no public record of it. Dr. Bright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:40.400
certainly did not pack the canteen with safe-class&nbsp;
humanoid SCPs and employees of the Foundation, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.960
ding a bell every five minutes so that eligible&nbsp;
singles could switch tables and meet someone new.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.080
There were no public displays of&nbsp;
affection on Foundation grounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.800
and certainly no ensuing disastrous&nbsp;
dates at any local Italian restaurants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:57.440
Dr. Bright is not allowed to organize&nbsp;
a speed dating event ever again. Um,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.920
I mean, for the first time. Because there&nbsp;
has never been one. Not here. No sir.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.040
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:11.200
He is not allowed to use&nbsp;
SCP-705 for personal gain!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.760
The Play-Doh toy soldiers are highly entertaining&nbsp;
to watch, and it’s understandable to be curious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:20.720
about their potential applications, but&nbsp;
Dr. Bright has taken it too far. He used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.880
the tiny soldiers to plant hidden cameras&nbsp;
and microphones in his colleague’s offices.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.200
Not only is this a violation of their&nbsp;
privacy, but it’s also just plain creepy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:34.400
and it’s unfair to make SCP-705 instances&nbsp;
accomplices to your bad behavior!

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.840
They didn’t know what they were signing&nbsp;
on to do, and if they’d known the hidden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:40.000
surveillance equipment was intended for&nbsp;
blackmail or for stealing a secret lasagna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.880
recipe that’s been in Dr. Giotta’s family for&nbsp;
generations, they never would have agreed.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.320
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:54.960
Dr. Bright is not permitted to assign the&nbsp;
designation “Over 9000” to any anomalies.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.520
Dr. Bright is to be reminded that first of&nbsp;
all, the SCP Foundation does not track the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.400
“power levels” of any of its anomalies,&nbsp;
as that is a completely subjective notion.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:10.240
Adding “it’s over 9000” to official&nbsp;
Foundation documents is distracting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:16.000
and confusing, particularly when applied to&nbsp;
entities like SCP-999 who have no interest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.120
in combat. Second of all, he should know that&nbsp;
joke hasn’t been relevant in over a decade, he’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:25.520
embarrassing himself and none of the new research&nbsp;
assistants even know what he’s referencing.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.680
Finally, he’s not as good at doing&nbsp;
the Vegeta voice as he thinks he is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.000
Update your references, Dr. Bright!&nbsp;
You’re better than that! …Maybe.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.360
Another Thing Dr. Bright Is Not&nbsp;
Allowed To Do At The Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.520
When writing a report, more detail is&nbsp;
expected than "Object class: Keter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:47.840
Special Containment Procedures: [DATA EXPUNGED].&nbsp;
Description: [DATA EXPUNGED]." And inventing new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:52.960
security clearances just so nobody can see what&nbsp;
you've written is also considered poor form.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.560
We all know sometimes RAISA can&nbsp;
get a little redaction-happy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.040
we understand the frustration, but that’s frankly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.360
no excuse to fill your documents with&nbsp;
nonsense and then hide them from us.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.800
If you keep doing this, we’ll send&nbsp;
Technical Researcher Rosen after you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.120
and we both know that guy’s a huge&nbsp;
jerk. Mark our words, Dr. Bright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:15.840
we are not bluffing - even if you do claim&nbsp;
to have Security Clearance Level 420!

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:23.040
Another Thing Dr. Bright Is Not Allowed To Do At&nbsp;
The Foundation: Showing Monty Python episodes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:30.160
SCP-239 was not a wise decision. Please never&nbsp;
try this with any other reality-warping SCP.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.920
Seriously, Dr. Bright. The Witch&nbsp;
Child is a reality warper so powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:38.720
we need to keep her in a comatose state to stop&nbsp;
her from permanently reformatting our universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.960
Do you really think it’s a good idea to&nbsp;
show her Flying Circus or the Holy Grail?

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.680
If we find that, by sheer coincidence, we&nbsp;
later need to contain an anomaly that shares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:52.480
a remarkable resemblance to the Black Beast&nbsp;
of Argh, we know exactly who is responsible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:58.320
and we will not take this indiscretion lightly.&nbsp;
We might even make you sit on the comfy chair!

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.680
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.840
Dr. Bright is Not Allowed to Kick SCP-2558-J!

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:11.040
SCP-2558-J refers to a group&nbsp;
of seemingly ordinary kittens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.120
who display friendly and affectionate&nbsp;
behavior toward humans and each other.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.040
When startled or made to feel afraid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:21.680
the kittens inflate into a fluffy spherical&nbsp;
shape about the size of a soccer ball,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:25.360
able to move around by rolling.
Dr. Bright is not permitted to kick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:30.160
any of the kittens, whether they are in&nbsp;
their ball form or not. He is also strictly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:36.800
prohibited from playing dodgeball, volleyball,&nbsp;
or any other ball-based game with SCP-2558-J.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:41.440
The only way anyone is permitted to play with&nbsp;
the kittens is using the Foundation-sanctioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:46.960
cat toys provided upon request. For&nbsp;
crying out loud, man, they're kittens!

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:50.880
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.120
Dr. Bright is Not Allowed to Play "Hippocratic&nbsp;
Oath Chicken" with the Medical Staff!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.800
The Hippocratic Oath is deeply&nbsp;
important to all medical professionals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:03.120
including those on staff at the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation. Dr. Bright is not permitted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.440
to try and convince the medical staff to&nbsp;
break the Hippocratic Oath in any way.&nbsp;

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:12.000
He is especially not allowed to expose them to&nbsp;
potentially dangerous anomalies while taunting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:18.160
"Still want to do no harm? You sure?" It's a waste&nbsp;
of time, resources, and it's just plain rude.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.200
One of these days, they're going to&nbsp;
snap and slap him across the face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.760
and not one of us will stop them.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.040
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:31.920
Dr. Bright! The Foundation Motto&nbsp;
is Not "Let's Use it on 682!"

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:37.360
Dr. Bright is to be reminded that the Foundation's&nbsp;
only official motto is Secure, Contain, Protect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:43.200
It is not, in fact, any of the alternatives he has&nbsp;
suggested. This includes but is not limited to:

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.960
"Can we put it in 914?"

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:47.520
"Blood makes the grass grow, kill, kill, kill!"

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.840
"Throw D-Class at it until it stops."

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.400
"When in doubt, feed it to 682."

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.600
"Slapstick, Clowns and Puns,"&nbsp;
or "Snap Crackle and Pop."

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.200
That last one got us served a cease&nbsp;
and desist from Kellogg's, and we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:03.200
can't afford a lawsuit right now. Cut it out!

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:10.080
A note to all SCP Foundation staff: If Dr. Bright&nbsp;
has to ask, it's above his clearance level.&nbsp;

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:13.360
If it's above Bright's security clearance… run.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:17.840
Dr. Bright is one of the SCP Foundation’s&nbsp;
most illustrious researchers, and as site&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:22.800
director of Site-19, there’s very little under&nbsp;
the Foundation's purview that he can’t do.&nbsp;

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:28.080
So if you find Dr. Bright is poking his stolen&nbsp;
nose where it shouldn’t be, then believe me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:32.320
you definitely shouldn’t be there. Think of&nbsp;
all the terrifying entities you know about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:39.200
from the SCP Foundation files. Now imagine all&nbsp;
the horrifying things you DON’T know about…

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:44.320
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed&nbsp;
to do at the Foundation: Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:50.080
allowed to send e-mails with memetic hazards&nbsp;
attached! No, not even when replying to spam!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:54.720
Dr. Bright. We don't care how annoying it is&nbsp;
when your inbox fills up with suspicious links,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.840
Linda's annoying Quote of The Day,&nbsp;
and chain letters telling you that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.520
you have to forward the email to 10&nbsp;
people or have bad luck for a year.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:06.000
That doesn't make it okay to&nbsp;
reply with SCP-2774 attached!

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.520
That goes for any other memetic&nbsp;
hazard. The last thing we need is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.200
more instances of these hazards&nbsp;
floating around in cyberspace.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:17.520
Take a breath, stand up from the keyboard,&nbsp;
and let the spam filter do its job.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:22.000
Another Thing Dr. Bright Is Not&nbsp;
Allowed To Do at The SCP Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:26.400
Dr. Bright cannot use “My evil&nbsp;
twin did it” as a viable excuse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:30.640
The same goes for “My good twin did&nbsp;
it”, considering the implication.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:35.200
Weirder things have happened at the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation than having an evil twin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:40.240
so maybe someone could make the excuse that their&nbsp;
evil twin committed some crime on their behalf.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:44.320
But the Bright family is one of the most&nbsp;
well-known dynasties in Foundation history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:48.480
so nobody is going to believe that there’s a&nbsp;
hidden member of the family still out there.&nbsp;

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:53.440
Maybe if SCP-963 had a perfect&nbsp;
copy, you might have an excuse here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:57.760
But to the best of our knowledge, that&nbsp;
is not the case. Take your lumps, Jack.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:02.080
Another Thing Dr. Bright Is Not&nbsp;
Allowed To Do At The SCP Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:07.520
Dr. Bright is not allowed to use “For The&nbsp;
Emperor” as justification for any decision.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.240
For starters, the SCP Foundation is independent&nbsp;
from the commands of any single nation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:16.400
It is an autonomous non-profit&nbsp;
organization, and you know that.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.920
Secondly, the only country in the world&nbsp;
that still has an active Emperor is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:25.200
Japan - and his role is purely ceremonial&nbsp;
because Japan is a constitutional monarchy.&nbsp;

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:29.440
And just for the record, “For the O5&nbsp;
Council” and “For The Administrator”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:33.680
are also unacceptable unless the order&nbsp;
you’re acting on actually comes from them.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:43.120
allowed to offer the solution of&nbsp;
"Use more guns" to any problem!

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:46.000
Dr. Bright. Look at me. We went over this before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:50.160
with the chainsaws. Do you remember?&nbsp;
Do we really need to do this again?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.200
I guess so.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.240
We face a wide variety of&nbsp;
problems here at the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:59.200
of varying degrees of severity. There is no&nbsp;
one-size-fits-all solution for these problems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:04.000
and even if there was, it would not be&nbsp;
"use more guns," or "get bigger guns."

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.440
This includes but is not limited&nbsp;
to: old-fashioned dueling pistols,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:12.320
machine guns, or something called the&nbsp;
"octo-gun" which my notes say was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:17.360
eight guns taped together...? How does that even&nbsp;
work? Never mind, don't answer that. The point is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:22.720
it's not helpful. And Dr. Bright is not allowed&nbsp;
in the armory. Not even on his birthday.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.800
The Ultimate Showdown
of Ultimate Destiny is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:33.440
not grounds to pit more than fifteen&nbsp;
combinative SCPs against each other!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:37.200
Okay, who let Dr. Bright log on to&nbsp;
YouTube unsupervised? Whoever it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.160
you're in big trouble because Dr.&nbsp;
Bright watched The Ultimate Showdown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:43.760
of Ultimate Destiny and it gave&nbsp;
him some pretty destructive ideas.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:48.320
Watching Batman fight Godzilla made him think&nbsp;
about throwing another giant lizard into combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:52.960
and he attempted to organize, in his&nbsp;
words, a Grand Tournament where fifteen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:57.280
of the most powerful and violent SCPs would&nbsp;
battle each other in a makeshift coliseum.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:03.120
This is not permitted, under any circumstances.&nbsp;
Yes, even if you film it and post it on YouTube.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:09.200
Another Thing Dr. Bright Is Not Allowed To Do&nbsp;
At The SCP Foundation: Yes, forum trolls are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:13.920
annoying. No, they don't automatically&nbsp;
become D-class personnel, Dr. Bright!

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:18.880
Personally, we’d think that someone who’s lived as&nbsp;
long as you - and died multiple times - would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:24.720
thicker skin. But your repeated insistence&nbsp;
to turn forumites like BootyHunter69 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:32.240
DankyDankyLiteratureClub420 into D-Class personnel&nbsp;
is as bizarre and sad as they are nonsensical.

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.360
People need to be truly despicable&nbsp;
to warrant having a place among the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:40.320
ranks of D-Class personnel. They need to&nbsp;
be truly monstrous, evil, underhanded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:45.520
unethical, bottom-of-the-barrel individuals,&nbsp;
and frankly, forum trolls do not fit the bill.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:48.080
YouTube Commenters, on the other hand…

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:52.560
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:57.520
No placing pranks in new staff's desks&nbsp;
and liquefying them in "record time!"

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.480
Starting a new job can be a stressful experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:03.920
Figuring out the office culture,&nbsp;
choosing a coffee cup in the break room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:08.080
and deciding which funko pops look best&nbsp;
on your desk, it's a lot to think about!

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:12.720
The last thing a new employee needs is to sit down&nbsp;
at their brand new desk, open a drawer to grab a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.680
pen, and have their flesh melted from their skull&nbsp;
by a bright blast of mysterious green light. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:23.280
not funny, we're not impressed anymore, and staff&nbsp;
turnover at the Foundation is already high enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:29.280
as it is. No more pranks, it's not a "right of&nbsp;
passage" if they don't survive it, Dr. Bright!!!

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:37.760
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed to do at&nbsp;
the Foundation: No unsupervised access to SCP-387!

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:44.880
SCP-387, or The Living Lego, is a miraculous&nbsp;
find. It is a tub of seemingly ordinary Lego&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:51.200
bricks that, when built into a shape by human&nbsp;
hands, comes to life and even develops sentience.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:56.800
Of course, Dr. Bright can never let a cool thing&nbsp;
just exist without wreaking some havoc with it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.800 --> 00:16:03.440
and decided to build a tiny lifelike model of&nbsp;
SCP-682. We have no idea how he built it so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:09.520
fast, or why it took military-grade explosives to&nbsp;
blow apart a creature made from plastic blocks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:14.480
but it was a mess to clean up, and Agent&nbsp;
Johnson will never get his big toe back.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:19.600
If Dr. Bright is so desperate to play with&nbsp;
Legos, he'll have to stick to the non-magic kind.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:23.120
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed to do:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:27.520
No bets concerning XK-Class&nbsp;
End of the World Scenarios!

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:31.600
It's the one thing we hope to&nbsp;
avoid: An XK Class Scenario,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:35.600
an event that results in the complete&nbsp;
and utter destruction of the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:40.800
Most of us prefer not to think about it at all,&nbsp;
unless we're actively trying to prevent it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:46.080
Not Dr. Bright, though. He sees the&nbsp;
apocalypse as a chance to make a quick buck!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:51.200
Dr. Bright is officially prohibited from making,&nbsp;
accepting, or taking any rake-off bets related to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:56.800
XK Class Scenarios. These include, but are not&nbsp;
limited to, "I'll bet you a thousand bucks the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:02.240
robots get us first," "it'll all start with&nbsp;
ducks," and "not with a bang, but with a whimper."

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:08.960
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed&nbsp;
to do: No showing bad movies to SCP-682!

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:16.640
SCP-682 is famous for a lot of things: its&nbsp;
indestructible nature, its insatiable appetite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:23.760
for violence, and the overflowing well of hate&nbsp;
in its heart. Unsatisfied with SCP-682's ordinary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:29.200
level of rage, Dr. Bright decided to take it upon&nbsp;
himself to give the lizard even more things to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:35.440
angry about, and organized an informal "so&nbsp;
bad it's good" film festival for the anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:42.000
and himself. The resulting damage, and loss of&nbsp;
life, cost the Foundation thousands of dollars.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.520
Movies on the "do not show to 682 list" include:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:52.000
The work of Uwe Boll, the work of Neil Breen,&nbsp;
The Room, Troll 2, Manos: The Hands of Fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:57.920
and, let's face it, any other movie Dr.&nbsp;
Bright can think of. No more movies.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:03.040
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed&nbsp;
to do at the Foundation: Dr. Bright is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:08.560
not allowed to classify any researcher,&nbsp;
including himself, as a memetic hazard!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:12.880
Memetic hazards are not to be taken&nbsp;
lightly. Many of the SCP Foundation's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:17.040
best and brightest have been cut down in&nbsp;
their prime by memetic hazards that ate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:20.400
away at their sanity and destroyed their minds.&nbsp;

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:25.280
Just because Dr. Bright likes singing "The&nbsp;
Song that Never Ends" and annoying everyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:30.560
that does not make him a memetic hazard by&nbsp;
Foundation standards. Other behaviors that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:35.040
do not qualify a researcher as a memetic&nbsp;
hazard include but are not limited to:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:41.120
whistling all the time, clipping their nails at&nbsp;
their desk, or microwaving fish in the break room.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:45.200
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:49.440
No claiming to be, or to&nbsp;
have ever been, Steve Irwin!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:56.400
How dare you? Steve Irwin was an international&nbsp;
treasure, and you will never, ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:04.400
fill his sensible shoes, Dr. Bright. No matter&nbsp;
how much you say "crikey" when looking at SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:10.320
no matter how many times you call it a "mighty big&nbsp;
croc!", no matter how much you photoshop yourself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:18.000
into photos of SCP-682 or how many Australians you&nbsp;
possess, you will never be The Crocodile Hunter.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:21.920
Stop trying to make it happen,&nbsp;
no one is going to call you that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:27.360
And stop tricking interns into buying autographed&nbsp;
memorabilia from you, we all know it's a forgery.

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:30.800
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:34.080
No changing the standard-issue D-Class uniform!

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:37.680
Dr. Bright is always proposing&nbsp;
changes at the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:40.800
and nearly all of them should&nbsp;
be disregarded immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:45.520
The D-Class uniform is perfect the way&nbsp;
it is, and does not need to be changed.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:49.520
It especially does not need to be changed&nbsp;
to black pants with a red polo shirt. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:54.800
get what you're going for, Dr. Bright. It's&nbsp;
very clever, we also enjoy Star Trek. But in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:59.280
addition to it being a waste of resources&nbsp;
to produce all of those new uniforms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:02.640
we just don't want a lawsuit from&nbsp;
Paramount Global on our hands.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:06.800
Another thing Dr. Bright is not&nbsp;
allowed to do at the Foundation:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:10.240
No playing Hot Potato with SCP-963!

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:16.400
SCP-963 is the ornate, anomalous amulet that&nbsp;
contains Dr. Jack Bright's consciousness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:20.880
Any living subject that comes into contact&nbsp;
with this amulet ceases brain function,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:24.160
and their consciousness is&nbsp;
replaced with Dr. Bright's.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:28.720
If they remain in contact with the amulet&nbsp;
for longer than 30 days, they will retain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:33.440
this consciousness even after the amulet has&nbsp;
been removed. Otherwise, they will experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:38.960
brain death. Essentially, it should be taken&nbsp;
incredibly seriously, and handled with great care.

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:44.000
It should not be tossed at a random D-Class,&nbsp;
Research Assistant, or any other Foundation staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:51.040
member with shouts of "CATCH!" or used to play any&nbsp;
other high-stakes contact-based game. It is not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:56.400
in fact, a "fun team-building exercise,"&nbsp;
that should be played on company retreats.

